{"id":"4d04b869450b424f","group":"89","path":"89/89-df-gl-complexity.md","title":"GL Complexity","display":"df-gl-complexity — GL Complexity","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"The Logic of Provability","book_abbrev":"89","label":"89-df-gl-complexity","aliases":["89-df-gl-complexity"],"display":"df-gl-complexity — GL Complexity","depends_on":["[[89-df-gl-algorithm]]","[[89-df-modal-formula]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"The Logic of Provability"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"89"},{"key":"label","html":"89-df-gl-complexity"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>89-df-gl-complexity</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-gl-complexity — GL Complexity"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"3bbdf6f3419b5805\" href=\"?note=3bbdf6f3419b5805\" title=\"89-df-gl-algorithm\">89-df-gl-algorithm</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"56c1b5b75a32ca1d\" href=\"?note=56c1b5b75a32ca1d\" title=\"89-df-modal-formula\">89-df-modal-formula</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\widehat d_{\\mathrm{GL}}\">\\(\\widehat d_{\\mathrm{GL}}\\)</span> is a fixed deterministic-machine implementation\nof the bounded search <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d_{\\mathrm{GL}}\">\\(d_{\\mathrm{GL}}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{enc}_{\\Box}:\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\\to\\Sigma^{*}\">\\(\\mathrm{enc}_{\\Box}:\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\\to\\Sigma^{*}\\)</span> is a fixed\ninjective effective encoding over a finite alphabet <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{steps}(\\widehat d_{\\mathrm{GL}},x)\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(\\mathrm{steps}(\\widehat d_{\\mathrm{GL}},x)\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span> is the number\nof steps used on input string <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\">\\(x\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Time}_{\\mathrm{GL}}:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb N\">\\(\\mathrm{Time}_{\\mathrm{GL}}:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb N\\)</span> 是下述定义的最坏运行步数函数，机器实现与公式编码均取上述固定选择。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}gl\\text{-}complexity}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Time}_{\\mathrm{GL}}(n)\n\\coloneqq\n\\max\\left(\n\\{\\mathrm{steps}(\\widehat d_{\\mathrm{GL}},\n\\mathrm{enc}_{\\Box}(A))\n\\mid A\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\\land\n|\\mathrm{enc}_{\\Box}(A)|\\le n\\}\n\\cup\\{0\\}\n\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}gl\\text{-}complexity}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Time}_{\\mathrm{GL}}(n)\n\\coloneqq\n\\max\\left(\n\\{\\mathrm{steps}(\\widehat d_{\\mathrm{GL}},\n\\mathrm{enc}_{\\Box}(A))\n\\mid A\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\\land\n|\\mathrm{enc}_{\\Box}(A)|\\le n\\}\n\\cup\\{0\\}\n\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Time}_{\\mathrm{GL}}\">\\(\\mathrm{Time}_{\\mathrm{GL}}\\)</span> records the worst-case running time of the\nchosen implementation and encoding; the finite alphabet makes the maximized\ninput set finite.</li>\n<li>PSPACE-completeness is a theorem about the decision problem, not part of this definition.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"89-df-gl-algorithm","status":"resolved","id":"3bbdf6f3419b5805","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnc